        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "The adverb: the word that never changes",
        "explicacao": "An adverb is a word that tells you HOW, WHEN, WHERE or HOW MUCH something happens: «well», «today», «here», «very». It never changes its form, not for gender and not for plural. That is the difference from the adjective: «хороший дом» (adjective: it changes with the noun) × «Он хорошо работает» (adverb: always «хорошо»). Many adverbs are born from an adjective: drop the ending (-ый, -ий, -ой) and add -о. Others are words in their own right: здесь, там, сейчас, очень, всегда.",
        "comparacao": "«quick» → «quickly», «slow» → «slowly». The idea is the same as in English: the adverb comes from the adjective and does not vary. In English you add -ly; in Russian you just swap the ending for -о.",
